A||||10||DJRice||Suggestions for Picture Posting||||3||
Z||000000||DJRice||02-03-2000||10:15 AM||||Lately, some very large pictures have been posted to the forum.  When these images are posted, sometimes the pages get difficult to read because they are 'wider' than the screen and one has to scroll from left to right to read a post.  Im bringing this up because this issue has been raised in several topics where large images have been posted, and I thought I might suggest a solution.  <P>Im sure that most of us are using a screen rez between 800*600 and 1280*1024.  Im thinking that for the convienence of all those viewing and reading the forums, we should try to keep the picture size to 800*600.  For those who are scanning pictures and dont end up with "standard" sizes, most of the photo editing programs have options to reduce picture size by a percentage which might be better so you dont ruin the length to width ratio of the picture.  If we can to this, not only will all of the pages be easier to read and enjoy, but it will also save Cliff's storage space and it will speed up download time.<P>As I said, this is just a suggestion. Im not trying to tell anyone how to post their pictures, but I think that things will work better if we can stick to 800*600 or less.<P>Just my $0.02||||reg||3
Z||000001||batboy||02-03-2000||12:37 PM||||Right on, bro!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Patrick||02-03-2000||03:31 PM||||<BR>I agree <B>DJ</B>, good suggestion. <P>I've got to the point where I just simply refuse to read posts in a thread where I have to scroll back and forth, left to right, to read them. ||||reg||14
